WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:02.940
What's happening?

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.310
De-fold signals!

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.560
We're detecting something immense!

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.020
It's a ship, but...

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:15.320
The wind is blowing.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.950
Let us begin, Heinz!

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.660
Yes.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.660
All ships, arm main turrets!

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.930
Fire!

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.720
What is this?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.390
What's happening?!

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:48.500
Impossible! The song of the wind is generating a dimensional rift!

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.550
I can hear it.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.810
Did something hap—

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.390
This song is...

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.360
It's the Wind Singer's.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.010
To all aerial units: belay the previous order.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:30.110
Abort launch preparations. I repeat.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.190
What's going on?!

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.540
Al-Shahal has fallen.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.530
What?!

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.990
It took less than fifteen minutes

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.870
and the NUNS forces stationed there have fallen silent.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.440
The power of the Protoculture...

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.370
is even greater than I thought.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.980
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.830
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.690
<i>Let's share a selfish kiss</i>

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:23.490
<i>The petals of this flower fall in the wind</i>

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:28.960
<i>The stars are more than I could count</i>

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.500
<i>I could place all the blame on you,</i>

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.250
<i>swallowing back my tears,</i>

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:40.090
<i>but I can't tell anyone about how my heart races</i>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.310
<i>(Reach out)</i>

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.600
<i>Until it all breaks apart</i>

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.550
<i>(Reach out)</i>

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.780
<i>Until you can take flight</i>

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.270
<i>(To the ends)</i>

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.150
<i>Deep in my heart</i>

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.890
<i>(Of time)</i>

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.690
<i>There is a prayer</i>

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.610
<i>Just feel, just believe</i>

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.710
<i>and speed through it all</i>

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.870
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.620
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:10.210
<i>Let's share a kiss faster than light, just wait for me</i>

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.840
<i>I'll leave my body behind</i>

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.840
<i>I'll leave my heart beating hard</i>

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.270
<i>I'll break free from these chains holding me down</i>

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:27.980
<i>Just come get me, in my purest form</i>

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.660
Glad to see you're still in one piece, mate.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.530
You too.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:49.390
{noise}The next battle's ours.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:50.840
{noise}We're gonna crush them.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.740
There are so many people...

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.920
Forces from all around the cluster have gathered here.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.800
And also survivors from the annexed planets.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.460
I see everyone's here.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:07.360
I see plenty of faces that bring back memories,

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.600
but we've got no time to chat about the old days.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.560
Let's begin the briefing.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.980
First, take a look at this.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:17.820
Is it a battleship?

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.530
I've never seen one like that.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.290
We believe this is Windermere's flagship.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:30.540
Judging by the waveform of its fold reactors, we suspect it was built 500,000 years ago by the Protoculture.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.200
The Protoculture?

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.420
Where did the Windermereans get that?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.980
We don't know.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:40.340
However, we detected bio-fold waves of unprecedented magnitude.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:44.550
It's extremely likely that the Wind 
Singer is on board that ship.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.570
The Wind Singer...

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:57.230
Just earlier, King Gramia VI of Windermere announced that they had liberated Al Shahal from NUNS.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.570
Their next target is definitely Ragna.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.320
His Majesty...

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.380
So they brought the head honcho along.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.280
They're going all in.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.320
The question is when.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.240
Not anytime soon.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:15.460
A song of such power must put 
a tremendous burden on its singer.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.080
How do you know?

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.710
I know best of all people.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:28.430
After using the song of the wind, they have never attacked in the following 24 hour time period.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.560
He who strikes first wins.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:35.390
We will ambush Al Shahal before the counter resets.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:38.690
Al Shahal? Why not Windermere?

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:45.360
Making a fold to Windermere is risky business due to the dimensional rift surrounding it.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.660
Also, King Gramia is at Al Shahal.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:54.120
The ambush will be carried out by the Ragnan forces, mainly the Delta Platoon and Walküre.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:58.860
We've been listening to Walküre's songs for a long time.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:02.460
Thus, we likely have a higher tolerance to the song of the wind than anyone else.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.680
All other units are to defend Ragna.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.370
Operation commences at 0400.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.800
That's all. Dismissed!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.440
First Lt. Mirage!

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.390
First Lt.?

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:19.140
You've been promoted.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.540
With this operation, you're my second-in-command.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.230
Your callsign will be Delta 2.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:27.340
I'm Delta 2?

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:35.950
I'm the aide to this operation's commander in chief, so I have to oversee all units.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.620
The Delta Platoon is in your hands.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.420
Don't make that face.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.840
We'll discuss the details later.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.300
I'm counting on you, First Lt. Mirage.

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.300
Yes, sir!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.380
Heinz?

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:01.030
Your Majesty. When will we advance into Ragna?

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:03.210
I can sing any time.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:04.320
Rest now.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.030
That is part of your duty as well.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.200
You did well, Heinz.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:15.700
Thank you.

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:23.880
During the attack on Al Shahal, we were able to further analyze an additional 10% of the ship's features.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.960
The Protoculture...

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.090
Ah, Lord Roid.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.050
Any problems with the shrine?

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.410
None whatsoever,

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.390
despite all the attacks targeted at us.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.350
What are you doing here?

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:43.120
You have no authority anymore.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.070
Stay put and watch over His Majesty and Prince Heinz.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:55.700
Prince Heinz cannot overexert himself anymore.

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:59.090
Our lives are short.

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:03.000
We can't have his rune run out.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.120
As long as we have the ruins and this ship,

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:09.380
we have a valid claim to being the heirs of the Protoculture.

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:13.150
We can negotiate with the NUNS on equal terms.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:19.060
They don't give a damn about the Protoculture.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:23.720
What about after the war is over?

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:27.660
There is so much we need to do. You and I both.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:28.610
We've got no time!

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:33.570
That is precisely why I'll fight until the very end,

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:39.400
even if I have to eradicate all 
earthlings in the cluster by myself.

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:43.120
I'll never forgive those who have tainted the wind.

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:50.250
I thought you'd fight until your last breath as well.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.490
Dying isn't the issue.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:02.830
But a new wind has yet to blow through the galaxy.

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:10.030
Sad rune.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.360
How are you feeling?

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.220
Worried about Windermere after all?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.860
The Wind Singer is at Al Shahal, right?

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:28.500
If our song reaches their heart, will 
they stop singing to control people?

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:31.930
Fre-Fre...

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.160
Will that wind flow through me again?

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:47.190
Captain. Preparing the shelters will take time.

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:49.110
Do it as fast as you can manage.

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:50.460
Roger.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:52.670
Are you evacuating civilians?

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.650
Expect the best, plan for the worst.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.360
How old is King Gramia?

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.830
He's over 35 now.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.910
He's lived long for a Windermerean.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.110
Tenacious bastard.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.880
Have you met him before, sir?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:14.040
You don't get to meet these kinds of 
people when you're just a NUNS pilot.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:14.970
So how?

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:16.890
He was a student of mine.

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.720
A student?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:24.350
At the time, I had been hired by Windermere to train them in fleet command.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:28.140
He was a horrible student.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:31.220
Always going on about chivalry.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:33.460
Fair and square, one-on-one.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:35.380
Not fleet command material, that's for sure.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:41.370
But he'll stop at nothing when it comes to defending his country and pride.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.030
He's a fearsome man.

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:46.020
What happened to you during their war of independence?

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:50.970
They wouldn't let an outsider get involved in their fight,

00:10:50.970 --> 00:10:53.540
so before the war began, I was dismissed.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:59.470
We fought. Orders are orders.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.590
Commander!

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:06.430
A NUNS ferry is asking for permission to land.

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.060
NUNS?

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:13.440
NUNS staff section two, Major Laurie Valan.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:18.400
Chaos Ragna division, captain 
of the Elysion, Ernest Johnson.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:24.340
You're even bigger than the stories sa—

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:26.450
To what do I owe the pleasure?

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:32.300
I'm delivering you a message from NUNS Central Command.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:36.460
The Protoculture ruins on planet 
Ragna are to be destroyed.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:43.820
Windermere is trying to use the 
ruins to gain control of the cluster.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:47.140
Destroying the ruins should render that impossible.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.140
So you send orders instead of reinforcements?

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:51.060
Said something?

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.150
Nothing, sir.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:58.060
Energy shafts extend into the 
planet's core from the ruins.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:01.320
Destroying them might cause severe changes in the planet's crust.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:05.270
We'll use a directed tactical reaction warhead.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:09.020
Collateral damage within the 
atmosphere should be minimal.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:12.040
Al Shahal fell in 15 minutes.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.920
Ragna won't last more than 30 either.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:18.880
Or do you have any better suggestions?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.090
I still cannot approve of that.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:28.170
I'm sure Lady M is of the same mind.

00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:31.520
I came to inform you so she could save face.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:35.310
We do not need your permission.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:39.450
Our special forces have already been dispatched.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.700
But...

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.370
We are ready to move.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.550
When do we strike Ragna?

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:58.840
Not yet. The wind is not blowing yet.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:02.510
Who is Ragna's commander?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:04.260
Ernest Johnson.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:10.040
He's a mercenary who's famous for always siding with the underdog.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:14.690
He's known as the commander who loses 100 out of 100 battles.

00:13:16.390 --> 00:13:18.940
A good opponent.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.570
We're not moving!

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:22.740
They're telling us to evacuate outta the blue!

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.240
Mom, I'm hungry!

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:37.600
Why do we have to evacuate?

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:40.460
Bro's team are going to beat 
up the bad guys, aren't they?

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:43.810
Looks like they're blowing up the ruins.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:47.290
Something might happen to Ragna.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.220
Like?

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.220
How should I know?

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.850
Damn those SOBs.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:58.400
Captain Arad?

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:02.480
Lady M talked with NUNS.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.150
Which means...

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:06.890
Good news.

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:11.320
They'll wait until our attack operation is over before blowing up the ruins.

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:13.080
Isn't that good, Rei-Rei?

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:15.630
What's wrong, Rei-Rei?

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:17.330
Being picky isn't good.

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:20.920
I like Ragna.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:25.210
I like mercats and sea spiders and sea scorpions.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.090
I like Ragnyannyan too.

00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:31.050
And I got to meet so many people here.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.010
You're right.

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:44.070
Let's protect Ragna.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.980
How should we fight the White Knight?

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.850
Freyja?

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:02.840
Freyja!

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.380
Ah, Hayate! Came to eat here too?

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:08.180
You can't fight on an empty stomach.

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.430
What are you having?

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.630
The all apple diet?

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:15.600
It's okay! They're Ragnan sea apples!

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:18.310
It's a bit salty but still delish!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.020
Why am I hiding?

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:24.680
It's been one crazy ride.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:25.270
Hm?

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:32.580
Who would've thought I'd end up fighting alongside the same stowaway I found back on Al Shahal?

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:35.000
True that!

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:38.310
By the way, what's that thing you're always wearing?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:41.790
A memento from my dad.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.920
From your dad?

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:49.100
He sent it from some planet when I was little.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:50.510
Which one?

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:53.330
Dunno. He was a soldier.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.980
He went wherever duty called.

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:00.980
Anyway, you actually became a member of Walküre.

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:05.650
And now my song might even reach Windermere.

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:07.390
Yeah.

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:13.070
Every now and then, singing is so much fun.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:14.470
Even during battles.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:14.990
Huh?

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:17.910
No, I mean... I know it's bad.

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:22.940
But the song wells up in me

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:25.600
and I can't help but enjoy it.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:32.670
If I could make people feel what I feel, 
maybe they'd never want to fight again.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.170
Maybe.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:40.260
Flying to your songs is lots of fun, too.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:40.890
Huh?

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:46.080
Even in the middle of a dogfight, it 
feels like I've suddenly grown wings

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.860
and I could fly as far as I want.

00:16:50.170 --> 00:16:54.200
It's vexing to admit, but I love your songs.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.760
So don't hold back. Sing with all you've got.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:01.830
I'm out there to protect you.

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:10.260
First Lt. Mirage, the meeting's about to start.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:11.790
Please come to the briefing room immediately.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.310
Crap!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:14.940
Mirage?

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:16.720
What are you doing there?

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.320
N-Nothing really.

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:20.680
I'm off.

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:22.850
Hold on, Delta 2.

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:26.740
Just because you're now second-in-command 
doesn't mean you always have to be so serious.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:27.350
Huh?

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.560
I'm talking about that.

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:33.920
I'm in charge now.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.570
I have to be prepared.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:36.820
You've got me.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:41.080
You've got Chuck and the captain.

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.780
We're here with you.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.220
Just fly like you always do.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.050
What's wrong?

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:57.720
I'm not talented like you are.

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:02.210
I've known that all along.

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:05.430
That's why I've been working twice as hard.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:08.280
Then First Lt. Messer would tell 
me off for flying by the book.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:12.560
But I can't just give up.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:15.150
I can't let it end here.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.280
Hayate Immelmann!

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:23.410
I lost to you during your final exam, but I'll be sure to pay you back someday.

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:26.330
So let's come back alive from this.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:28.060
Yeah.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:30.710
I'll wait for your challenge, Second Lieutenant.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:53.250
Macross Elysion, standby for launch.

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:56.830
I repeat. Macross Elysion, standby for launch.

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.200
Hurry with the weapon system checks!

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.720
Inertial capacitor, check.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.870
Main reactor output increasing.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.350
Activating gravity control systems.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.090
Mooring systems unlocking.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.260
Launch area, all clear.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:25.060
Macross Elysion, commence ascent.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.150
I'm Ernest Johnson, captain of the Macross Elysion

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:41.170
and commander in chief of Chaos, 
Brisingr Globular Cluster Combined Fleet.

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:46.070
Operation Einherjar begins now.

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:52.000
Let's show them some real yak deculture!

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:56.210
Macross Elysion, full speed ahead!

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:15.730
Wow!

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:18.690
It's the Macross Elysion!

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:23.920
Commencing transformation.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:27.620
Main engine blocks switching to outer space cruising mode.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:31.800
Aether and Hemera tails locked to main hull.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.890
Exited atmosphere.

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:39.120
Fold drive charging complete.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.010
All units, fold!

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:55.150
A storm is coming.

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:58.220
Spread our wings.

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:05.050
Once we de-fold, Walküre will start an 
assault concert toward the enemy fleet.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:07.420
For the galaxy...

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:08.480
For someone out there...

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:09.700
We will...

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.990
go all out...

00:21:11.990 --> 00:21:13.910
and enjoy ourselves!

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.370
The Delta Platoon will cover Walküre.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:22.020
All other units are to launch a focused attack on the giant enemy warship.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:24.490
I'm counting on you to kick some ass!

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:28.280
De-fold in 20 seconds.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:32.530
19. 18. 17.

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:33.560
No way...

00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:36.600
We're detecting a massive body at our destination.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:37.560
Approaching rapidly!

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:39.930
A massive body?

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:43.320
Are they planning to—

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:53.450
The enemy fleet are executing a fold!

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:56.210
Good one, Gramia.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:22:00.920
Shall we begin?

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:06.680
Mission 12: King of the Wind

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:08.520
Are you ready?

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:26.700
<i>I heard a rumor that the world's gonna end someday</i>

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:32.210
<i>Just kidding, it's obviously a lie</i>

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:37.550
<i>I remember looking up at the sky</i>

00:22:37.550 --> 00:22:41.260
<i>and feeling like I was in the future</i>

00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:46.860
<i>I felt completely in sync with your wind</i>

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:55.860
<i>You make me truly feel like a girl</i>

00:22:55.860 --> 00:23:03.360
<i>so I've got no choice but to do it. I can't stop now!</i>

00:23:03.360 --> 00:23:04.950
You better be ready!

00:23:04.950 --> 00:23:08.540
<i>If my rune shines with a flash</i>

00:23:08.540 --> 00:23:12.290
<i>wow woh wow woh</i>

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:15.780
<i>I fall in love</i>

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:19.250
<i>wow woh wow woh</i>

00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:24.800
<i>Lalali lalala you make me</i>

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:32.590
<i>Lalala rune pika invincible</i>

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:39.600
Next time: Passionate Diving
